[# decorative/background-pattern: a section with a repeating pattern or texture image behind its content.

   MJML writes a VML fallback for Outlook desktop, so the pattern still shows there. The solid background color is
   what people see when images are blocked, so keep it close to the pattern's tone and keep the message in text.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: background image via the VML fallback MJML generates. Repeat patterns tile.
   - Gmail apps: background images can be blocked or dropped in some clients, the solid color shows instead.
   - Dark mode: the pattern and its background color stay as they are, they are a branded block. #]
<mj-section[[ cc(cls) ]] background-color="[[ s.background ]]" background-url="[[ data.pattern ]]" background-repeat="[[ s.repeat ]]" background-size="[[ s.size ]]" padding="[[ s.padding ]]">
  <mj-column>
    [[ data.content ]]
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
